# Rust
target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed — Pane ships as a binary, so reproducible
# transitive-dep resolution matters. A silent semver bump to a broken
# minor release otherwise takes the CI matrix down (happened on
# 2026-06-14 with alloc-stdlib 0.2.3).

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# Tauri
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
src-tauri/WixTools/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Local
.env
.env.local

# Sidecar binaries (fetched per-platform), except the helper APK which
# is built+committed by .github/workflows/helper-apk.yml so the desktop
# release pipeline can bundle it without chaining cross-workflow artifacts.
# Glob the dir contents instead of the dir itself — git can't re-include
# a file underneath an ignored directory.
src-tauri/binaries/*
!src-tauri/binaries/pane-helper.apk

# Test artefacts
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Android helper APK build output
tools/pane-helper-android/.gradle/
tools/pane-helper-android/build/
tools/pane-helper-android/app/build/
tools/pane-helper-android/local.properties
tools/pane-helper-android/.idea/
# Local Claude Code state stays out of the repo, but the skills under it are
# shared tooling: versioning them means every clone and every worktree gets the
# same guidance, instead of it living only on one machine.
# Note the trailing /* — git never descends into an excluded *directory*, so a
# plain `.claude/` would make the negations below unreachable.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
